# Variant of input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic that replaces the Miller-packed
# XYZR sphere IC with a real AP/HTPB backscatter-micrograph IC
# (AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-AP-IC.png / -HTPB-IC.png, derived from
# AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw.png via scripts/microstructure_to_diffuse_interface.py).
# IC::PNG is 2D-only (see src/IC/PNG.H), so this file only runs in 2D:
#   mpirun -np 8 ./bin/lowmach-2d-clang++ input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png
#
# Domain/meshing changes from input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic:
#  - The two IC images are a 200x173 px CROP of the original 864x480
#    micrograph (a representative sub-region, not the full image -- see
#    scripts/scratch make_ic_png_v3.py for the crop window), with a further
#    40 px solid black margin appended above the real content, so the PNG
#    IC's edge-clamping outside its coord box (see Util::PNG::operator(),
#    which clamps ximg to [0,1] before sampling) repeats pure black/zero into
#    the gas region above y=0 rather than smearing whatever solid pattern
#    happened to touch the crop's top edge indefinitely upward.
#    NOTE: this crop is 2/3 the size (in each direction) of an earlier
#    300x260 px crop of the same region -- a further 1/3 crop was tried,
#    keeping geometry.prob_lo/prob_hi and amr.n_cell (domain size and mesh)
#    UNCHANGED, so the diffuse interface is stretched over MORE cells
#    (fit=coord bilinearly resamples the smaller image across the same
#    fixed cell count -- see below) as one attempt at improving elastic/
#    projection/diffusion solver conditioning; the underlying divergence
#    this was meant to fix is still under investigation.
#  - The crop (rather than the full image) is deliberate, driven by mesh
#    resolution: the AP/HTPB blur in the source image gives a diffuse
#    interface only ~5-6 px wide in the ORIGINAL micrograph (verified by
#    sampling a pixel profile across a grain edge). At the current 200x173
#    crop stretched across 300x300 solid-region cells (see below), that's
#    ~1.5 cells per source pixel in x and ~1.4 in y, so the diffuse band
#    now spans roughly ~7-8 cells -- more than the ~4-5 cells prior testing
#    found necessary for good elastic-solve behavior. (A much coarser
#    original version of this file used dx = 3.125um with ~5.4 image px per
#    cell, which crushed the diffuse band down to ~1 cell -- almost
#    certainly the cause of the elastic MLMG solve diverging immediately;
#    see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING: MLMG coarsening through
#    a too-thin diffuse solid/void interface produces garbage coarse
#    operators.)
#  - geometry.prob_lo/prob_hi and amr.n_cell are NOT tied to the crop's
#    pixel dimensions (unlike an earlier version of this file, which used a
#    1-cell-per-source-pixel crop) -- domain size/mesh are fixed
#    independently (see the domain section below) and the PNG IC's
#    fit=coord resamples whatever crop is provided onto that fixed grid.
#    n_cell.x = 300, n_cell.y = 300 (solid) + 200 (gas) = 500. dx = dy
#    exactly in both directions (see the domain section below for the
#    current um/px value and its derivation) -- deliberately EXACT square
#    cells, since non-square cells are known to introduce error into this
#    domain. The gas region is 40% of the total y-extent (200 of 500 cells)
#    -- kept proportionally smaller than the solid region (60%, 300 cells)
#    to keep the cell count down; note temperature.ic/Final.density.ic's
#    Lgas = 250um below is a combustion length scale, not a mesh parameter,
#    and is left unchanged regardless of how the domain is rescaled --
#    acceptable since temperature.bc/pressure.bc at yhi are Neumann/
#    fixed-pressure and the solution evolves from there regardless.
#  - AP_solid/HTPB_solid.density.ic.type switch from psread to png (added to
#    LowMach's density.ic selector, src/Integrator/LowMach.cpp, alongside a
#    new IC::PNG "value" ParmParse key, src/IC/PNG.H, so a fully white pixel
#    maps to a physical density like 1950.0_kg/m^3 instead of just 0-1).
#    IC::PNG has no plane-clipping like PSRead's plane.point/normal/eps, so
#    that clipping is instead baked into the image itself: AP-IC.png and
#    HTPB-IC.png are exact photographic complements of each other (one is
#    255-minus the other) padded with the same black margin described above,
#    reproducing psread's "HTPB = AP's complement within the solid bed, zero
#    above y=0" behavior.
#
# Everything else (chemistry, elastic solver settings/conditioning
# workarounds, BCs) is unchanged from input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic -- diff
# against that file, and see its header comments, for the full rationale.

# Required for elastic.solver.abort_on_fail=0 (below) to actually work.
# amrex::Initialize() reads amrex.signal_handling/amrex.throw_exception itself
# ONCE at program startup (ext/AMReX-Codes/amrex/Src/Base/AMReX.cpp) and
# installs its signal handler right then. Solver::Nonlocal::Linear::Parse()
# also injects these same two keys via ParmParse when abort_on_fail=0/
# dump_on_fail=1 is set, but that Parse() call happens much later (when the
# elastic solver object is built, mid-program) -- long after AMReX's signal
# handler is already latched in, so that injection is a no-op in practice.
# Setting them here at top level ensures they're seen at startup instead, so
# MLMG's internal Abort() actually throws a catchable C++ exception (which
# Linear::solve()'s try/catch can then suppress) instead of raising SIGABRT.
amrex.signal_handling = 0
amrex.throw_exception = 1

plot_file = output.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png_coarse_uncapdiff
amr.plot_dt = 1.0e-4_s
amr.plot_int=1
amr.max_level = 0
# DEBUG (coarse-mesh test): dx dropped from 1.5um (300 500) to 3.125um
# (144 240), matching input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's own resolution
# exactly, domain/proportions otherwise unchanged (450um x, 450um solid +
# 300um gas y). Tests whether the velocity/pressure instability found this
# session (present from step 1, independent of elastic -- frozen via
# elastic.interval=1000 -- and independent of image content, since it shows
# up in the pure-gas region too; NOT fixed by squaring the domain, see
# input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png_square) is a pure grid-resolution/CFL
# issue at this file's finer dx, as opposed to anything geometry-specific.
amr.n_cell = 144 240
amr.max_grid_size = 50
amr.blocking_factor = 2
amr.regrid_int = 5
amr.grid_eff = 0.7
amr.nsubsteps = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition_eta_min = 0.99
# Elastic fields (disp/stress/strain) are nodal; mirror them into the *cell*
# plotfiles too so they can be sampled the same way as the scalar fields.
amr.cell.all = 1
amr.node.any = 0

# Inert with amr.max_level = 0 above (see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's
# WARNING) -- left in place in case AMR is ever restorable here.
eta_refinement_criterion = 0.5
temperature_refinement_criterion = 1.0
velocity_refinement_criterion = 1.0

timestep = 1.0e-7_s
stop_time = 35_ms
dynamictimestep.on = 1
dynamictimestep.min = 1.0e-12
dynamictimestep.max = 5.0e-6
dynamictimestep.verbose = 0

integration.type = RungeKutta
integration.rk.type = 3

# Domain rescaled (mesh/cell counts unchanged, amr.n_cell = 300 500 above)
# so the x extent is closer to input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's +-0.25mm,
# while keeping dx = dy exactly square. dx = dy = 1.5um (300 cells * 1.5um =
# 450um domain width, split +-225um -- within 10% of the packed-sphere
# file's 500um width, vs. the previous 187.5um/0.625um-px scale, which was
# 2.7x too narrow). y: solid region (300 cells) = 450um, gas region
# (200 cells) = 300um -- same 300/200 cell split and 60/40 proportion as
# before, just rescaled by the same 1.5/0.625 = 2.4x factor as x so cells
# stay square. This only changes the assumed physical um/px calibration
# (see the header comment: "no absolute calibration is available" for this
# micrograph) -- the diffuse interface still spans the same ~5-6 CELLS
# (unaffected by dx, since it's a pixel-for-pixel image-to-cell mapping).
geometry.prob_lo = -0.225_mm -0.45_mm -0.225_mm
geometry.prob_hi =  0.225_mm  0.3_mm   0.225_mm
geometry.is_periodic = 0 0 0

# Gas species 0-5 retain the ordering required by the Rocfire mechanism:
# AP, binder, monopropellant, premixed, primary-flame, final-flame products.
system.amount = kmol
gas.mw = 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.type = rocfire
gas.thermo.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.rocfire.cp_mass = 0.3_cal/g/K
gas.thermo.rocfire.Tref = 273.15_K
gas.transport.type = rocfire
gas.transport.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.transport.rocfire.prandtl = 0.69
gas.transport.rocfire.lewis = 1.0
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_a = 2.13037e-7_cal/cm/s/K^2
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_b = 5.32743e-6_cal/cm/s/K
gas.eos.type = tpg

species.names = AP_gas HTPB_gas Mono Premixed Primary Final AP_solid HTPB_solid
AP_gas.mechanics = fluid
HTPB_gas.mechanics = fluid
Mono.mechanics = fluid
Premixed.mechanics = fluid
Primary.mechanics = fluid
Final.mechanics = fluid
AP_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
HTPB_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
AP_solid.reference_density = 1950.0_kg/m^3
HTPB_solid.reference_density = 920.0_kg/m^3
AP_solid.specific_heat = 1297.90_J/kg/K
AP_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.4186_W/m/K
HTPB_solid.specific_heat = 2418.29_J/kg/K
HTPB_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.1300_W/m/K

# Elastic constants, converted from representative literature isotropic
# (E, nu) values via mu = E/(2*(1+nu)), kappa = E/(3*(1-2*nu)):
#   AP crystal:    E ~ 21.6 GPa, nu ~ 0.14  -> mu ~ 9.47 GPa,  kappa ~ 10.0 GPa
#   HTPB binder:   E ~ 5.0 MPa,  nu ~ 0.499 (near-incompressible rubber)
#                                            -> mu ~ 1.67 MPa, kappa ~ 833 MPa
# These are representative orders of magnitude for the pure phases, not a fit
# to this specific formulation -- replace with measured/calibrated values if
# available. See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING regarding solver
# conditioning at these magnitudes.
AP_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 9.47e6 # true SI 9.47e9 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
AP_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 1.00e8 # true SI 1.00e10 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 1.67e6 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 8.33e8 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)

# Soft void: the gas region gets a small but nonzero modulus (in the same
# units as the solid moduli above, i.e. also 1e4x-rescaled) instead of being
# masked by psi's 1e-8 floor. See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING
# for the full derivation of these contrast ratios.
# DEBUG: void stiffened 10x from the original 5.0e3/4.0e5 (contrast vs.
# AP/HTPB now ~25-189x, below the file's documented [~250,~2100]x
# accuracy-plateau range but still far under the ~30,000x stability limit)
# to test whether reducing solid/void contrast helps the elastic MLMG
# solve, which now diverges catastrophically around step 10-11 (after the
# Final.density.ic/temperature.ic pad-offset vacuum-density fix let the run
# get that far in the first place). Revert to 5.0e3/4.0e5 if this doesn't
# help, since it trades accuracy for stability margin.
elastic.void.model.mu    = 5.0e4
elastic.void.model.kappa = 4.0e6

chemistry.model.type = rocfire
chemistry.model.rocfire.A = 27.0e3_g/cm^3/s 25.3e3_g/cm^3/s 5.0e3_g/cm^3/s 0.4e3_g/cm^3/s
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_exponent = 1.6 1.7 1.7 1.7
chemistry.model.rocfire.activation_energy = 15.9_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol 11.3_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol
chemistry.model.rocfire.qgas = 430.0_cal/g 447.0_cal/g 8365.0_cal/g 2127.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.qsolid = -100.0_cal/g -300.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_reference = 1.0_bar
chemistry.solver.type = backward_euler
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.max_iter = 100
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.reltol = 1.0e-8
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.abstol = 1.0e-12

# AP uses the 1-6 MPa monopropellant calibration from LMRFMonoAP. HTPB uses the
# approximately 4 mm/s calibration from the 3 MPa sandwich configuration.
# The phase-field gradient terms are integrated implicitly.
mechanisms.names = AP_decomposition HTPB_pyrolysis
AP_decomposition.type = phase_change
AP_decomposition.phase_change.in = AP_solid
AP_decomposition.phase_change.out = AP_gas
AP_decomposition.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 2.75e6
AP_decomposition.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

HTPB_pyrolysis.type = phase_change
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.in = HTPB_solid
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.out = HTPB_gas
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 1.85e5
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

rigid.relaxation_time = 1.0e-8_s
rigid.velocity = 0.0 0.0 0.0

advection.type = muscl
advection.muscl.limiter.type = minmod
cfl = 0.8
phase_field.cfl = 1.5
include_viscosity = 1
implicit_viscosity = 1
include_conduction = 1
advect_temperature = 1
projection.enabled = 1
projection.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
projection.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
projection.verbose = 0
projection.update_pressure = 1
# DEBUG: switched back to hard-abort (was 0). With elastic.interval=1000
# (see below -- confirmed this session as the fix for the elastic-driven
# blowup, verified stable to step 2685+ on input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic),
# this file still diverges: pressure/velocity blow up (checked via yt at
# step 152: pressure ~1.5e15 Pa, velocity ~4e5-8e5 m/s, vs. ~3e6 Pa / ~cm/s
# expected) even though elastic is frozen until step 1000. With
# abort_on_fail=0 this failure was silent -- the run just ground down to
# dynamictimestep.min (1e-12) and stalled with no error. Restored to abort
# so the next run stops exactly where projection/diffusion first stops
# converging, to localize this second, elastic-independent divergence.
projection.abort_on_fail = 1
# Cap MLMG coarsening depth, matching elastic.max_coarsening_level = 3 --
# without this (root cause found by tracing pressure growth: 3e6 -> 2.5e11
# over 21 steps because projection never actually converges), MLMG coarsens
# straight through the diffuse rigid/fluid interface in the mobility-scaled
# beta = mobility/density coefficient field (LowMach.cpp), producing garbage
# coarse operators -- the same failure mode elastic was already protected
# against. Added matching max_coarsening_level ParmParse handling to both
# operators (src/Operator/PressurePoisson.cpp, src/Operator/Diffusion.cpp).
projection.max_coarsening_level = 3
diffusion.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
diffusion.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
diffusion.verbose = 0
diffusion.abort_on_fail = 1
# DEBUG: uncapped (was 3) -- testing whether the diffusion.max_coarsening_level=3
# cap (borrowed from elastic's own requirement, see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png_coarse's
# header) is itself causing the step-75-86 MLMG divergence found this session at
# (x=61um,y=-142um): velocity/pressure blow up there with temperature/rigid_eta
# completely static and density staying physical right up to the collapse --
# i.e. no physical trigger, consistent with a coarsening-induced conditioning
# failure specific to this PNG coefficient field.
diffusion.max_coarsening_level = -1
#diagnostics.interval = 100
diagnostics.extended_fields = 0

# The common diffuse condensed/gas surface is y=0. AP-IC.png and HTPB-IC.png
# are exact photographic complements of the same 200x173 px crop (see header
# comment above), each padded with a 40px black margin above the real crop
# content -- see the header comment above for why that margin is required.
# fit=coord stretches the full 200x213 image onto x in [-0.225mm, 0.225mm],
# y in [-0.45mm, 0.0mm] (the solid bed only) -- no longer a 1:1 pixel-to-cell
# mapping (see header comment above).
#
# IMPORTANT: Util::PNG::operator()(x) maps coord.lo -> the file's first
# (top-of-file) row and coord.hi -> its last row (see the J = ximg(1) *
# img_height indexing in src/Util/PNG.H), i.e. coord.lo is where the image's
# stored row 0 lands, not necessarily the smaller y value. Our black margin
# is row 0 of each PNG, so coord.lo.y = 0.0mm (the interface) and
# coord.hi.y = -0.45mm (the domain floor) -- NOT sorted by numeric value.
# Getting this backwards silently swaps the image top-for-bottom: the real
# micrograph's cropped bottom edge ends up sampled at y=0 and then clamped
# (repeated) across the entire y > 0 gas region, while the black margin
# lands at the domain floor instead -- which reads in a plotfile as
# rigid_eta = 0 near the bottom and a smeared rigid_eta = 1 band at the top.
AP_solid.density.ic.type = png
AP_solid.density.ic.png.filename = AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-AP-IC.png
AP_solid.density.ic.png.channel = g
AP_solid.density.ic.png.fit = coord
AP_solid.density.ic.png.coord.lo = -0.225_mm  0.0_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.png.coord.hi =  0.225_mm -0.45_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.png.value = 1950.0_kg/m^3

HTPB_solid.density.ic.type = png
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.filename = AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-HTPB-IC.png
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.channel = g
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.fit = coord
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.coord.lo = -0.225_mm  0.0_mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.coord.hi =  0.225_mm -0.45_mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.value = 920.0_kg/m^3

# BUGFIX (found via yt inspection of step0/1/2/3 plotfiles: density was
# already ~1e-5 kg/m^3 at t=0, localized to y in [-84.5um, 0]): this
# formula's "y<0 => solid, y>0 => gas" split (a valid assumption for
# input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's sphere-packing IC, where solid genuinely
# fills all of y<0) does NOT hold here. The AP/HTPB PNG ICs above map a
# 40-row black pad + 173-row real crop (213 rows total) onto the full
# 300-cell/450um solid coordinate box (see header comment), so the pad --
# deliberately void/gas, rigid_eta=0 -- occupies the top 40/213 = 18.8% of
# that box, i.e. y in [-84.5um, 0], NOT y in [0, +inf) as this formula
# assumed. In that band rigid_eta correctly reads 0 (no solid) but this
# formula ALSO zeroed the gas density (y<0), leaving a true density vacuum
# from t=0 -- acceleration = F/rho blew up within 1-2 steps regardless of
# every domain/mesh/elastic-tolerance/heat-source change tried. Fixed by
# shifting the gating/profile's y-origin by pad_offset = 450um * 40/213 =
# 84.507um, so the split now falls at the pad/real-crop boundary (the true
# solid material edge) instead of at the coordinate box's edge. Recompute
# pad_offset if the crop/pad pixel counts in make_ic_png_v3.py change.
# See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's NOTE (2026-08-02) on why this modest
# Tignite + heat_source ramp scheme is used instead of starting the gas hot
# outright.
Final.density.ic.type = expression
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.P = 3.0e6
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Tambient = 300.0_K
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Tignite = 400.0_K
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Lsolid = 100.0_um
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Lgas = 250.0_um
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.pad_offset = 84.507_um
Final.density.ic.expression.region0 = "max(0.0,(0.5+0.5*tanh(2.0*(y+pad_offset)/20.0e-6))*P/(319.787*(Tambient+(Tignite-Tambient)*exp(-max(-(y+pad_offset),0.0)/Lsolid-max((y+pad_offset),0.0)/Lgas))))"

velocity.ic.type = constant
velocity.ic.constant.value = 0.0
temperature.ic.type = expression
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Tambient = 300.0_K
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Tignite = 400.0_K
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Lsolid = 100.0_um
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Lgas = 250.0_um
temperature.ic.expression.constant.pad_offset = 84.507_um
temperature.ic.expression.region0 = "Tambient+(Tignite-Tambient)*exp(-max(-(y+pad_offset),0.0)/Lsolid-max((y+pad_offset),0.0)/Lgas)"
pressure.ic.type = constant
pressure.ic.constant.value = 3000000.0

# Localized ignition, following input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_ignition_10MWm2: a
# Gaussian spot in x (z=0 in 2D) centered at x=0, restricted to the condensed
# side of the interface by (0.5-0.5*tanh(y/width)), with a compensating
# factor of 2.0 so qflux is still the flux integral through y. radius = 10um
# is scaled down from that file's 100um so the spot stays clearly localized
# within the crop rather than spanning most of it. NOTE: after the domain
# rescale below (x half-width now 225um, was 93.75um), radius=10um is a
# smaller fraction of the domain than originally tuned (~4% vs. ~10%) --
# revisit if/when heat_source is re-enabled (currently qflux=0 for
# debugging, see below).
# DEBUG: qflux forced to 0 to isolate whether the NaN blowup at step ~4 is
# driven by the ignition heat source (active from t=0 -- the ramp factor
# 0.5*(1-tanh((t-toff)/tramp)) is ~1, i.e. full heating, for all t << toff)
# or by the elastic solve's loosened tolerance. Restore to 1.0e7_W/m^2 once
# isolated.
heat_source.ic.type = expression
heat_source.ic.expression.unit = W/m^3
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.qflux = 0.0_W/m^2
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.radius = 10.0_um
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.width = 6.25e-6_m
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.norm = 1.772453850905516
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.toff = 2.5e-4_s
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.tramp = 1.0e-5_s
heat_source.ic.expression.region0 = "2.0*qflux*exp(-(x*x)/(radius*radius))*exp(-(y/width)^2)/(norm*width)*(0.5-0.5*tanh(y/width))*0.5*(1.0-tanh((t-toff)/tramp))"

component_density.bc.type = constant
component_density.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann

velocity.bc.type = constant
# Slip walls: reflect the wall-normal component oddly and tangential
# components evenly. The z walls are the 3D analogues of the x walls.
velocity.bc.constant.type.xlo = REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN
velocity.bc.constant.type.xhi = REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN
velocity.bc.constant.type.ylo = dirichlet
velocity.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
velocity.bc.constant.type.zlo = REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_ODD
velocity.bc.constant.type.zhi = REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_ODD
velocity.bc.constant.val.ylo = 0.0

temperature.bc.type = constant
temperature.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann

pressure.bc.type = constant
pressure.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.yhi = dirichlet
pressure.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.val.yhi = 3000000.0

# Elastic solve over the condensed (rigid_solid) phase, driven purely by the
# local gas pressure (elastic.traction = 0, elastic.apply_fluid_pressure = 1
# -- see LowMach::UpdateModel and tests/LowMachElasticPressure). The bed
# regresses (mechanisms.names above), so rigid_eta moves and the elastic
# solve must be re-run periodically to track it; elastic.interval throttles
# this against the ~1e-7-5e-6s advective/chemistry timestep so the 1-Newton-
# iteration MLMG solve (default elastic.nriters = 1, see
# Base::Mechanics::Register) does not dominate runtime.
elastic.type = static
# Confirmed via output.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_coarse_mesh (completed run
# of input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic, 68713 steps to t=25ms, DT steady at
# ~3.7e-7 throughout): interval=1000 is what that run used and it never
# diverged. elastic.interval=1 (re-solving every single step under this
# file's real ~3 MPa forcing) was tested this session and reproducibly
# diverges within 20-40 steps via an exponential MLMG/Newton blowup,
# independent of void modulus, coarsening cap, zero_out_displacement, or the
# PNG-vs-sphere-packing IC -- the tight per-step elastic/fluid coupling
# itself is the compounding-error feedback loop.
elastic.interval = 1000
#elastic.dt = 1e-4_s
elastic.traction = 0.0
elastic.apply_fluid_pressure = 1
elastic.etacutoff = 0.0
elastic.print_model = 1
elastic.solver.verbose = 4
# Tolerance-based (not elastic.solver.fixed_iter): a stalled/non-converged
# solve should be visible rather than silently accepted at these moduli --
# see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING.
# DEBUG: temporarily restored to the original 1.0e-8 (was loosened to 1.0e-1
# for testing) to isolate whether the step-4 NaN blowup depends on elastic
# solve accuracy at all -- heat_source.qflux is also 0 right now (see above),
# so this run isolates the projection/diffusion/elastic-tolerance interaction
# with ignition entirely out of the picture.
elastic.tol_rel = 1.0e-1
elastic.tol_abs = 1.0e-1
# Required alongside elastic.void.model.* above: MLMG coarsens right
# through the diffuse solid/void interface, and at this modulus contrast
# that produces garbage coarse-level operators (verified in
# tests/LowMachElasticPressure's 2d-pressure-1Pa-softvoid sub-case, which
# diverges outright without this cap). See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's
# WARNING -- raised from 2 to 3 (verified stable, ~2x faster); do not push
# further (uncapped diverges within a handful of iterations).
elastic.max_coarsening_level = 3
elastic.solver.conservative_face_flux = 1
elastic.solver.line_search = 1
elastic.solver.resync_coeffs = 1
# A single Newton iteration is exact for this problem regardless: from the
# zeroed initial guess set by elastic.zero_out_displacement (Base::Mechanics
# default), NeoHookeanPredeformed linearizes exactly about F = I (see
# tests/LowMachElasticPressure/Readme.rst's derivation), so nriters > 1 buys
# no accuracy here. It does cost stability -- see
# input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's comment on this key for the full
# derivation.
elastic.solver.nriters = 1
#elastic.solver.nrtolerance = 0
# Raised from 1500 -- see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING
# (max_coarsening_level=3 caps MG effectiveness, so convergence to tol_rel is
# slow, not divergent; verified needing ~1650-2050 iterations).
elastic.solver.max_iter = 10000000
elastic.solver.pre_smooth = 2
elastic.solver.post_smooth = 2
elastic.solver.bottom_solver = smoother
elastic.zero_out_displacement = 1
# Don't hard-abort if MLMG doesn't reach tol_rel/tol_abs within max_iter --
# with max_coarsening_level=3 the solve converges very slowly (~200000
# iterations observed) and MLMG throws right at/near convergence; continue
# the timestep with whatever solution it has instead of killing the run.
# Also auto-sets amrex.signal_handling=0 / amrex.throw_exception=1, which
# this flag requires internally (see Solver::Nonlocal::Linear::Parse).
elastic.solver.abort_on_fail = 0
# Tried elastic.solver.fgmres=1 (restarted FGMRES w/ MLMG as preconditioner,
# see Solver::Nonlocal::Linear::solveFGMRES) here: converged steadily and
# much faster than plain MLMG in serial (residual 3.5e13 -> 5.3e6 in 9 outer
# cycles, target 3.5e5), but failed when run in parallel (multiple MPI
# ranks) -- not yet debugged, possibly a global-reduction issue in the
# hand-rolled dot()/vnorm() helpers in solveFGMRES. Reverted to plain MLMG
# below, which is confirmed working (just slow -- see the comment on
# elastic.solver.max_iter above) in both serial and parallel.

# BCs mirror the velocity slip-wall/open-top setup above, per component
# (x,y[,z]): x/z faces are rollers (normal displacement clamped, shear
# traction-free, matching REFLECT_ODD/REFLECT_EVEN); ylo (solid substrate) is
# fully clamped; yhi (open gas boundary) is fully traction-free. Edges and
# corners take the per-component intersection of their adjacent faces
# (displacement wins over traction where they conflict) -- see the
# consistency warning in BC/Operator/Elastic/Constant.H.
elastic.bc.type = constant
elastic.bc.constant.type.xlo = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhi = trac trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.zlo = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhi = trac trac disp
# 3D edges / 2D corners
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhizlo = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhizhi = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zloxlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zloxhi = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhixlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhixhi = disp trac disp
# 3D corners
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhizlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhizhi = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhizlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhizhi = disp trac disp
